# LeakSanitizer suppressions for MaBoSS.
#
# Scope: this file contains only what is needed to keep the *gating* sanitizer
# job -- the unit tests -- clean. It is a to-do list, not a permanent
# exemption; delete each entry as the leak behind it is fixed.
#
# Applied automatically by ctest for a -DMABOSS_SANITIZE=... build, or by hand:
#     LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=engine/tests/sanitizers/lsan.supp
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parser leaks (~190 bytes per parse, in ~12 allocations)
#
# The flex/bison actions allocate with new/strdup and do not free on every
# path: BooleanGrammar.y:290 and :295, BooleanGrammar.l:112 and :120,
# RunConfigGrammar.y:343, RunConfigGrammar.l:80.
#
# Harmless for the command line tools, which parse one model and exit. It does
# accumulate for long-lived processes that parse repeatedly -- the cmaboss
# Python module and ensemble runs -- which is why it is worth fixing rather
# than suppressing forever.
leak:ctbndlparse
leak:ctbndllex
leak:rcparse
leak:rclex

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT suppressed
#
# These show up when the regression tests run under ASan. They are left
# unsuppressed on purpose: suppressing them would need a pattern broad enough
# (`leak:main`) to hide real leaks too. The regression-test sanitizer job is
# therefore reporting-only until they are fixed.
#
#   engine/src/MaBoSS.cc:838   `new Network()` and the RunConfig beside it are
#                              not freed on every exit path (416 bytes, seen in
#                              the ensemble test).
#
#   engine/src/engines/ProbTrajEngine.cc:278 and :280
#                              buildSchedule() allocates the per-node schedule
#                              expressions and never frees them (480 bytes in
#                              10 objects, seen in the schedule test).
